{"type":"text","timestamp":1790452448358,"sessionID":"ses_f20bf47cfffeV6ijDzFg5cPuFL","part":{"id":"prt_0df483c4d0011xFuQTLo2pgWsb","messageID":"msg_0df480544001MURBlC0qleBTR0","sessionID":"ses_f20bf47cfffeV6ijDzFg5cPuFL","type":"text","text":"Done. I created both the **BattleOverPanel scene** and its **script**, and verified they work.\n\n### `res://scenes/ui/battle_over_panel.tscn`\n- Root `Panel` named `BattleOverPanel` with `process_mode = Always (3)` and full-rect anchors (`anchor_right = 1.0`, `anchor_bottom = 1.0`).\n- Panel style overridden with a `StyleBoxFlat` using `bg_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 0.47)`.\n- A centered `VBoxContainer` with anchors at `0.5` and offsets `-36/-36/36/36`.\n- `Label` (unique) with text `\"Encounter Won\"`, horizontal & vertical center alignment, and `LabelSettings` with `font_size = 31`.\n- `ContinueButton` and `RestartButton` (unique), each with `custom_minimum_size = (80, 28)`, `size_flags_horizontal = Expand (4)`, and texts `\"Next Round\"` / `\"Reset Fight\"`.\n\n### `res://scenes/ui/battle_over_panel.gd`\n- `class_name BattleOverPanel` extending `Panel`.\n- `enum Type { WIN, LOSE }`.\n- `@onready` bindings via `%Label`, `%ContinueButton`, `%RestartButton`.\n- In `_ready`, connects `ContinueButton.pressed` → `get_tree().quit`, `RestartButton.pressed` → `get_tree().reload_current_scene`, and `Events.battle_over_screen_requested` → `show_screen`.\n- `show_screen(text, type)` updates the label, toggles `ContinueButton` on WIN and `RestartButton` on LOSE, shows the panel, and pauses the scene tree.\n\nI verified the behavior by running the scene in Godot: the panel displays correctly, the toggle logic works (both buttons shown on default load, only ContinueButton shown after a WIN event), and the tree pause is applied.","time":{"start":1790452448333,"end":1790452448337},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"resp_1b4f5995fa7d4dc99b50f90c109d47e8_msg"}}}}
